{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FjxKEVkadE9iJK35Dw3fKb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have very detailed per-segment data. Let me compile the APC 300 per-segment breakdown:\n\n**Segment 0** (main segments):\n- STARK excl trace: 602ms\n- Trace Commit: 107ms\n- Constraints: 390ms\n  - LogUp GKR: 203ms (input_evals: 96ms)\n  - Round 0: 104ms (PLE round0: 95ms)\n  - MLE Rounds: 83ms\n- Openings: 103ms\n  - Stacked Reduction: 37ms (R0: 14ms, MLE: 23ms)\n  - WHIR: 65ms\n\n**Segment 1** shows similar patterns but slightly faster across most components—STARK excl trace drops to 523ms, constraints come in at 335ms with LogUp GKR at 166ms, and the openings phase takes 97ms including a 60ms WHIR step. The leaf recursion phase is starting to appear in the data.\n\nNow I'm looking at the breakdown for the leaf recursion and internal phases—leaf recursion STARK excl trace is 287ms, and the internal phases add another 92ms. But when I sum up just the main segments (602ms from segment 0 plus 523ms from segment 1), I get exactly 1125ms, which matches what spec.py reports. That means the 1125ms figure only accounts for the app proof itself, not the recursive layers on top of it.\n\nLooking at the GKR metrics more closely, I can see that segment 0's GKR inner rounds are about 107ms (203ms total minus 96ms for input evals), and segment 1's are roughly 106ms (166ms total minus 60ms for input evals). Across both segments, that's around 213ms of inner rounds, which aligns with the total GKR time of 369ms minus the combined input eval time of 156ms. Now I need to examine how this breaks down at APC 0 for each segment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1708,"cache_read_input_tokens":92454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1708},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"