{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0116S8vQmocQS5gBgvwFMXNM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TKSbFzpJV2ggg6p9AZUEFB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute\n\nInline the `precompute_logup_combinations` GPU kernel computation into the `logup_monomial_kernel` to eliminate 1582 redundant kernel launches and ~55ms of separate GPU compute per proof. Currently, each MLE sumcheck round launches separate precompute kernels that compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t)` for every monomial, writing to intermediate buffers that the monomial evaluation kernel then reads. Since the monomial kernel already accesses the MonomialHeader (which contains `num_terms`/`term_offset`) and the required data (`d_eq_3bs`, `d_terms`) is already on the device, the combination can be computed inline with negligible overhead (~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds per monomial), eliminating the intermediate buffer allocation, the H2D/D2H traffic, and the precompute kernel launches entirely.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":183889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":638},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"ab9262f6-7958-469b-b46a-7cd86897c221"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TKSbFzpJV2ggg6p9AZUEFB","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"9d2e7c60-1459-4803-83df-68c6c6c542fc","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:07:20.623Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute\n\nInline the `precompute_logup_combinations` GPU kernel computation into the `logup_monomial_kernel` to eliminate 1582 redundant kernel launches and ~55ms of separate GPU compute per proof. Currently, each MLE sumcheck round launches separate precompute kernels that compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t)` for every monomial, writing to intermediate buffers that the monomial evaluation kernel then reads. Since the monomial kernel already accesses the MonomialHeader (which contains `num_terms`/`term_offset`) and the required data (`d_eq_3bs`, `d_terms`) is already on the device, the combination can be computed inline with negligible overhead (~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds per monomial), eliminating the intermediate buffer allocation, the H2D/D2H traffic, and the precompute kernel launches entirely.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction","+# 2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute"," ","-Move the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (iDFT + polynomial multiplication + accumulation) from CPU to GPU using a multi-kernel pipeline with `batch_ntt_small` and existing AoS/SoA conversion primitives. The current CPU-side `reconstruct_s0_from_g` / `ntt_multiply_and_add` pipeline performs per-bucket D2H transfers (each syncing the stream), followed by serial iDFT, DFT, pointwise multiplication, and inverse DFT on the host. Moving this to GPU eliminates ~18 redundant stream syncs and ~60-80 CPU NTT operations, replacing them with batched GPU NTT calls that complete in microseconds.","+Inline the `precompute_logup_combinations` GPU kernel computation into the `logup_monomial_kernel` to eliminate 1582 redundant kernel launches and ~55ms of separate GPU compute per proof. Currently, each MLE sumcheck round launches separate precompute kernels that compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t)` for every monomial, writing to intermediate buffers that the monomial evaluation kernel then reads. Since the monomial kernel already accesses the MonomialHeader (which contains `num_terms`/`term_offset`) and the required data (`d_eq_3bs`, `d_terms`) is already on the device, the combination can be computed inline with negligible overhead (~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds per monomial), eliminating the intermediate buffer allocation, the H2D/D2H traffic, and the precompute kernel launches entirely."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-16-0830-gpu-stacked-reduction-poly-extraction\n\nMove the Stacked Reduction Round 0 polynomial reconstruction (iDFT + polynomial multiplication + accumulation) from CPU to GPU using a multi-kernel pipeline with `batch_ntt_small` and existing AoS/SoA conversion primitives. The current CPU-side `reconstruct_s0_from_g` / `ntt_multiply_and_add` pipeline performs per-bucket D2H transfers (each syncing the stream), followed by serial iDFT, DFT, pointwise multiplication, and inverse DFT on the host. Moving this to GPU eliminates ~18 redundant stream syncs and ~60-80 CPU NTT operations, replacing them with batched GPU NTT calls that complete in microseconds.\n"}}
