rrent performance"},{"content":"Profile the system with nsight","status":"completed","activeForm":"Profiling the system"},{"content":"Research source code for bottleneck root causes","status":"completed","activeForm":"Researching source code"},{"content":"Generate and rank optimization ideas","status":"completed","activeForm":"Generating optimization ideas"},{"content":"Write task.md with selected optimization","status":"completed","activeForm":"Writing task.md"},{"content":"Write plan.md with detailed implementation plan","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Writing plan.md"},{"content":"Get plan reviewed by subagent and iterate","status":"pending","activeForm":"Getting plan reviewed"},{"content":"Final verification checklist","status":"pending","activeForm":"Verifying final checklist"}],"verificationNudgeNeeded":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0165puMza5oirdVTSh9ECS2n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014evzE2PaNeeZCqHoVHj3Yh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Inline Logup Combination Precompute\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate the separate `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel` GPU launches by computing logup combination values inline within the `logup_monomial_kernel`. This targets 55ms of GPU compute time (33% of MLE Rounds) caused by 1582 tiny kernel launches that each compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t)` per monomial, writing to intermediate buffers that the monomial kernel then reads back. The monomial kernel's `MonomialHeader` already contains `num_terms`/`term_offset`, and the required data (`d_eq_3bs`, `d_terms`, `d_beta_pows`) is already on the device, so the computation can be done inline with ~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds per monomial.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Precompute phase (per MLE round, per eval group)\n\n1. **Rust caller** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs:509-579`): `compute_logup_combinations()` called per AIR. For each AIR:\n   - Allocates `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for `d_numer_combinations` (line 524-525)\n   - Allocates `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for `d_denom_combinations` (line 543-544)\n   - Launches `precompute_logup_numer_combinations` FFI (line 531)\n   - Launches `precompute_logup_denom_combinations` FFI (line 550)\n   - Computes `bus_term_sum` on CPU (line 568-573)\n\n2. **CUDA kernel** (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu:304-327`): `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<IS_DENOM>` — one thread per monomial. Each thread:\n   - Reads `MonomialHeader` from `headers[m]` (has `num_terms`, `term_offset`)\n   - Loops over `hdr.num_terms` terms, reading `InteractionMonomialTerm` from `terms[hdr.term_offset + t]`\n   - Computes `sum += eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient` (numer) or `sum += eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient * beta_pows[term.field_idx]` (denom)\n   - Writes result to `out[m]`\n\n3. **FFI wrappers** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:1333-1363`): `precompute_logup_numer_combinations()` and `precompute_logup_denom_combinations()`.\n\n### Consumption phase (batch monomial MLE evaluation)\n\n4. **Batch setup** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs:607-`): `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` takes `logup_combinations: &[&LogupCombinations]` and builds per-AIR `LogupMonomialCtx` structs with `d_combinations` pointer to the precomputed buffer.\n\n5. **CUDA kernel** (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu:393-442`): `logup_monomial_kernel<IS_DENOM>` — one block per (y_int, mono_block). Each thread:\n   - Reads `MonomialHeader` from `ctx.d_headers[m]` (line 421) — same struct, already has `num_terms`/`term_offset`\n   - Reads precomputed combination: `FpExt monomial = ctx.d_combinations[m]` (line 422)\n   - Loops over `hdr.num_vars` variables, multiplying monomial by evaluated variable (lines 423-426)\n   - Multiplies by `eq_xi[y_int]` and reduces (lines 427-441)\n\n### Data structures\n\n- **`MonomialHeader`** (`cuda/include/monomial.cuh:19-24`): `{var_offset: u32, term_offset: u32, num_vars: u16, num_terms: u16}` — 12 bytes. Both precompute and monomial kernels use the same struct.\n- **`InteractionMonomialTerm`** (`cuda/include/monomial.cuh:37-41`): `{coefficient: Fp, interaction_idx: u16, field_idx: u16}` — 8 bytes.\n- **`LogupMonomialCtx`** (`batch_mle_monomial.cu:376-381`): `{d_headers, d_variables, d_combinations, num_monomials}`.\n- **`LogupMonomialCommonCtx`** (`batch_mle_monomial.cu:368-374`): `{eval_ctx, d_eq_xi, bus_term_sum, num_y, mono_blocks}`.\n- **`InteractionMonomials`** (`pkey.rs:68-78`): Keygen-time data. Contains `d_numer_terms`/`d_denom_terms` (device buffers of `InteractionMonomialTerm`) that persist for the entire proof.\n\n### Nsight profile (APC 300)\n\n- `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<true>`: 35ms GPU, 791 instances, 44μs avg\n- `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<false>`: 20ms GPU, 791 instances, 25μs avg\n- Total: 55ms GPU time, 1582 kernel launches\n- MLE Rounds total: 161ms wall time → precompute is 34% of MLE Rounds\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Extend `LogupMonomialCtx` and `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` (CUDA)\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`\n\nReplace the `d_combinations` field in `LogupMonomialCtx` with `d_terms`:\n\n```c++\nstruct LogupMonomialCtx {\n    const MonomialHeader *__restrict__ d_headers;\n    const PackedVar *__restrict__ d_variables;\n    const InteractionMonomialTerm *__restrict__ d_terms;  // was: d_combinations\n    uint32_t num_monomials;\n};\n```\n\nAdd `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` to `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`:\n\n```c++\nstruct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_xi;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_3bs;     // NEW\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_beta_pows;  // NEW (null for numer-only AIRs)\n    FpExt bus_term_sum;\n    uint32_t num_y;\n    uint32_t mono_blocks;\n};\n```\n\n**Why:** These pointers give the monomial kernel access to the data it needs to compute combinations inline. The `d_terms` pointer replaces `d_combinations` because the terms array (already on device from keygen) contains the interaction_idx and coefficient data.\n\n### Change 2: Inline combination computation in `logup_monomial_kernel` (CUDA)\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`\n\nReplace line 422 (`FpExt monomial = ctx.d_combinations[m]`) with inline computation:\n\n```c++\n// Compute combination inline instead of reading from precomputed buffer\nFpExt monomial(Fp::zero());\nfor (uint16_t t = 0; t < hdr.num_terms; ++t) {\n    InteractionMonomialTerm term = ctx.d_terms[hdr.term_offset + t];\n    FpExt value = FpExt(term.coefficient) * common_ctx.d_eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx];\n    if constexpr (IS_DENOM) {\n        value *= common_ctx.d_beta_pows[term.field_idx];\n    }\n    monomial += value;\n}\n```\n\n**Why:** This replaces a single global memory read (`d_combinations[m]`) with 1-3 iterations of: one global memory read (`d_terms[offset+t]`) + one global memory read (`d_eq_3bs[idx]`) + 1-2 FpExt multiplications. The term data is small (8 bytes per term), and `d_eq_3bs` has high temporal locality (same indices accessed across monomials in the same AIR). The net compute overhead per monomial is ~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds, negligible compared to the variable evaluation loop (lines 423-426).\n\n### Change 3: Update Rust `LogupMonomialCtx` and `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` repr(C) structs\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nUpdate the Rust `LogupMonomialCtx` struct to match the new CUDA layout:\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct LogupMonomialCtx {\n    pub d_headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n    pub d_variables: *const PackedVar,\n    pub d_terms: *const InteractionMonomialTerm<F>,  // was: d_combinations: *const EF\n    pub num_monomials: u32,\n}\n```\n\nUpdate `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`:\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n    pub eval_ctx: EvalCoreCtx,\n    pub d_eq_xi: *const EF,\n    pub d_eq_3bs: *const EF,      // NEW\n    pub d_beta_pows: *const EF,   // NEW\n    pub bus_term_sum: EF,\n    pub num_y: u32,\n    pub mono_blocks: u32,\n}\n```\n\n**Why:** Rust repr(C) structs must match the CUDA struct layout exactly for correct FFI.\n\n### Change 4: Update `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` to pass terms + eq_3bs instead of combinations\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n\nModify `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` (line ~607):\n\n1. Change the signature: remove `logup_combinations: &[&LogupCombinations]` parameter. Add `d_eq_3bs: &DeviceBuffer<EF>` and `d_beta_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>`.\n\n2. When building per-AIR `LogupMonomialCtx`, set `d_terms` from the keygen data (`pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.interaction_monomials.d_numer_terms` / `d_denom_terms`) instead of `logup_combinations[i].d_numer_combinations`.\n\n3. When building `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`, set `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` from the new parameters.\n\n**Why:** The terms data lives in the proving key (keygen-time, persisted for the full proof). By pointing directly to this data, we avoid allocating and populating per-round combination buffers.\n\n### Change 5: Remove `compute_logup_combinations()` calls from MLE round loop\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs` and callers\n\n1. Remove all calls to `compute_logup_combinations()` within the MLE round loop. This function is currently called per-AIR per-round, producing `LogupCombinations` that are passed to `LogupMonomialBatch::new()`.\n\n2. Keep the `bus_term_sum` CPU computation (lines 568-573) since it's cheap and the monomial kernel still needs it.\n\n3. Update the call sites of `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` to pass `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` instead of `logup_combinations`.\n\n**Why:** This eliminates the 1582 precompute kernel launches and their DeviceBuffer allocations.\n\n### Change 6: Remove precompute kernel and FFI (cleanup)\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`: Remove `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel`, `_precompute_logup_numer_combinations`, `_precompute_logup_denom_combinations` functions.\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`: Remove FFI declarations and safe wrappers for the precompute functions.\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`: Remove `LogupCombinations` struct and `compute_logup_combinations()` function.\n\n**Why:** Dead code removal. The precompute path is fully replaced by inline computation.\n\n### Change 7: Update the initial precompute overlap with Round 0\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (the `overlap-logup-precompute-round0` code path)\n\nThe existing code spawns `compute_logup_combinations()` on a background thread concurrent with Round 0. Since `compute_logup_combinations()` is being removed, this background thread no longer needs to precompute combinations. However, it still needs to:\n- Upload `d_eq_3b` per trace (this is still needed by the inline kernel)\n- Precompute `bus_term_sum` per AIR on CPU\n\nUpdate the background thread to skip the precompute kernel launches but retain the `d_eq_3b` upload and `bus_term_sum` computation. Store the `bus_term_sum` values for later use by `LogupMonomialBatch::new()`.\n\n**Why:** The background thread's precompute was overlapping with Round 0 to hide latency. With inline computation, the precompute GPU work disappears, but the `d_eq_3b` upload and CPU `bus_term_sum` computation are still needed.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: The inline combination computation must produce exactly the same `FpExt` values as the separate precompute kernel. Both paths compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t * [beta_pows[field_idx_t] if IS_DENOM])`. Verify by running all 94 tests.\n\n2. **Struct layout**: Rust `repr(C)` structs must match CUDA structs byte-for-byte. Field order and types must be identical. The `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` now has 2 extra pointer fields (16 bytes) — ensure the Rust and CUDA definitions agree on padding.\n\n3. **No regression at APC 0**: At APC 0, the monomial MLE path processes fewer monomials. The inline computation adds negligible overhead per monomial, so no regression is expected. Verify empirically.\n\n4. **Keygen data lifetime**: The `d_numer_terms` / `d_denom_terms` device buffers in `InteractionMonomials` must remain valid for the entire proof. They currently do (owned by the proving key). The monomial kernel's `d_terms` pointer must not outlive this data.\n\n5. **bus_term_sum correctness**: The CPU-computed `bus_term_sum` must still be passed correctly to `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`. This value depends on `eq_3bs` which changes per MLE round, so it must be recomputed per round.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build: `cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"` (from powdr repo)\n2. Run APC 0, 100, 300 benchmarks (from `powdr/results/pairing/`):\n   ```\n   powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apcXXX.cbor --input 0 --metrics <output>.json --recursion\n   ```\n3. Analyze with `spec.py` — focus on:\n   - MLE Rounds time at APC 300 (expect: ~106-121ms, down from 161ms)\n   - STARK excl trace at APC 300 (expect: ~1070-1085ms, down from 1125ms)\n   - APC 0 MLE Rounds (expect: no regression, ~117ms unchanged)\n4. Run nsight profile for APC 300:\n   - Verify `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel` instances = 0\n   - Verify `logup_monomial_kernel` time increase is < 5ms\n5. Run full test suite: `cargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4`\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 is < 20ms (below noise floor for this component)\n- Revert if APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by > 20ms\n- Revert if any test fails\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":185004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"ab7b88bb-5a8e-4dfb-8a14-c67393c4d28d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014evzE2PaNeeZCqHoVHj3Yh","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute/plan.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"b0daf1e7-ba9b-4927-95db-6931679a3595","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:08:46.722Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Inline Logup Combination Precompute\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate the separate `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel` GPU launches by computing logup combination values inline within the `logup_monomial_kernel`. This targets 55ms of GPU compute time (33% of MLE Rounds) caused by 1582 tiny kernel launches that each compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t)` per monomial, writing to intermediate buffers that the monomial kernel then reads back. The monomial kernel's `MonomialHeader` already contains `num_terms`/`term_offset`, and the required data (`d_eq_3bs`, `d_terms`, `d_beta_pows`) is already on the device, so the computation can be done inline with ~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds per monomial.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Precompute phase (per MLE round, per eval group)\n\n1. **Rust caller** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs:509-579`): `compute_logup_combinations()` called per AIR. For each AIR:\n   - Allocates `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for `d_numer_combinations` (line 524-525)\n   - Allocates `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for `d_denom_combinations` (line 543-544)\n   - Launches `precompute_logup_numer_combinations` FFI (line 531)\n   - Launches `precompute_logup_denom_combinations` FFI (line 550)\n   - Computes `bus_term_sum` on CPU (line 568-573)\n\n2. **CUDA kernel** (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu:304-327`): `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<IS_DENOM>` — one thread per monomial. Each thread:\n   - Reads `MonomialHeader` from `headers[m]` (has `num_terms`, `term_offset`)\n   - Loops over `hdr.num_terms` terms, reading `InteractionMonomialTerm` from `terms[hdr.term_offset + t]`\n   - Computes `sum += eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient` (numer) or `sum += eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient * beta_pows[term.field_idx]` (denom)\n   - Writes result to `out[m]`\n\n3. **FFI wrappers** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:1333-1363`): `precompute_logup_numer_combinations()` and `precompute_logup_denom_combinations()`.\n\n### Consumption phase (batch monomial MLE evaluation)\n\n4. **Batch setup** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs:607-`): `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` takes `logup_combinations: &[&LogupCombinations]` and builds per-AIR `LogupMonomialCtx` structs with `d_combinations` pointer to the precomputed buffer.\n\n5. **CUDA kernel** (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu:393-442`): `logup_monomial_kernel<IS_DENOM>` — one block per (y_int, mono_block). Each thread:\n   - Reads `MonomialHeader` from `ctx.d_headers[m]` (line 421) — same struct, already has `num_terms`/`term_offset`\n   - Reads precomputed combination: `FpExt monomial = ctx.d_combinations[m]` (line 422)\n   - Loops over `hdr.num_vars` variables, multiplying monomial by evaluated variable (lines 423-426)\n   - Multiplies by `eq_xi[y_int]` and reduces (lines 427-441)\n\n### Data structures\n\n- **`MonomialHeader`** (`cuda/include/monomial.cuh:19-24`): `{var_offset: u32, term_offset: u32, num_vars: u16, num_terms: u16}` — 12 bytes. Both precompute and monomial kernels use the same struct.\n- **`InteractionMonomialTerm`** (`cuda/include/monomial.cuh:37-41`): `{coefficient: Fp, interaction_idx: u16, field_idx: u16}` — 8 bytes.\n- **`LogupMonomialCtx`** (`batch_mle_monomial.cu:376-381`): `{d_headers, d_variables, d_combinations, num_monomials}`.\n- **`LogupMonomialCommonCtx`** (`batch_mle_monomial.cu:368-374`): `{eval_ctx, d_eq_xi, bus_term_sum, num_y, mono_blocks}`.\n- **`InteractionMonomials`** (`pkey.rs:68-78`): Keygen-time data. Contains `d_numer_terms`/`d_denom_terms` (device buffers of `InteractionMonomialTerm`) that persist for the entire proof.\n\n### Nsight profile (APC 300)\n\n- `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<true>`: 35ms GPU, 791 instances, 44μs avg\n- `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<false>`: 20ms GPU, 791 instances, 25μs avg\n- Total: 55ms GPU time, 1582 kernel launches\n- MLE Rounds total: 161ms wall time → precompute is 34% of MLE Rounds\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Extend `LogupMonomialCtx` and `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` (CUDA)\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`\n\nReplace the `d_combinations` field in `LogupMonomialCtx` with `d_terms`:\n\n```c++\nstruct LogupMonomialCtx {\n    const MonomialHeader *__restrict__ d_headers;\n    const PackedVar *__restrict__ d_variables;\n    const InteractionMonomialTerm *__restrict__ d_terms;  // was: d_combinations\n    uint32_t num_monomials;\n};\n```\n\nAdd `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` to `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`:\n\n```c++\nstruct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_xi;\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_3bs;     // NEW\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_beta_pows;  // NEW (null for numer-only AIRs)\n    FpExt bus_term_sum;\n    uint32_t num_y;\n    uint32_t mono_blocks;\n};\n```\n\n**Why:** These pointers give the monomial kernel access to the data it needs to compute combinations inline. The `d_terms` pointer replaces `d_combinations` because the terms array (already on device from keygen) contains the interaction_idx and coefficient data.\n\n### Change 2: Inline combination computation in `logup_monomial_kernel` (CUDA)\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`\n\nReplace line 422 (`FpExt monomial = ctx.d_combinations[m]`) with inline computation:\n\n```c++\n// Compute combination inline instead of reading from precomputed buffer\nFpExt monomial(Fp::zero());\nfor (uint16_t t = 0; t < hdr.num_terms; ++t) {\n    InteractionMonomialTerm term = ctx.d_terms[hdr.term_offset + t];\n    FpExt value = FpExt(term.coefficient) * common_ctx.d_eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx];\n    if constexpr (IS_DENOM) {\n        value *= common_ctx.d_beta_pows[term.field_idx];\n    }\n    monomial += value;\n}\n```\n\n**Why:** This replaces a single global memory read (`d_combinations[m]`) with 1-3 iterations of: one global memory read (`d_terms[offset+t]`) + one global memory read (`d_eq_3bs[idx]`) + 1-2 FpExt multiplications. The term data is small (8 bytes per term), and `d_eq_3bs` has high temporal locality (same indices accessed across monomials in the same AIR). The net compute overhead per monomial is ~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds, negligible compared to the variable evaluation loop (lines 423-426).\n\n### Change 3: Update Rust `LogupMonomialCtx` and `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` repr(C) structs\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nUpdate the Rust `LogupMonomialCtx` struct to match the new CUDA layout:\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct LogupMonomialCtx {\n    pub d_headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n    pub d_variables: *const PackedVar,\n    pub d_terms: *const InteractionMonomialTerm<F>,  // was: d_combinations: *const EF\n    pub num_monomials: u32,\n}\n```\n\nUpdate `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`:\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n    pub eval_ctx: EvalCoreCtx,\n    pub d_eq_xi: *const EF,\n    pub d_eq_3bs: *const EF,      // NEW\n    pub d_beta_pows: *const EF,   // NEW\n    pub bus_term_sum: EF,\n    pub num_y: u32,\n    pub mono_blocks: u32,\n}\n```\n\n**Why:** Rust repr(C) structs must match the CUDA struct layout exactly for correct FFI.\n\n### Change 4: Update `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` to pass terms + eq_3bs instead of combinations\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n\nModify `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` (line ~607):\n\n1. Change the signature: remove `logup_combinations: &[&LogupCombinations]` parameter. Add `d_eq_3bs: &DeviceBuffer<EF>` and `d_beta_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>`.\n\n2. When building per-AIR `LogupMonomialCtx`, set `d_terms` from the keygen data (`pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.interaction_monomials.d_numer_terms` / `d_denom_terms`) instead of `logup_combinations[i].d_numer_combinations`.\n\n3. When building `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`, set `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` from the new parameters.\n\n**Why:** The terms data lives in the proving key (keygen-time, persisted for the full proof). By pointing directly to this data, we avoid allocating and populating per-round combination buffers.\n\n### Change 5: Remove `compute_logup_combinations()` calls from MLE round loop\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs` and callers\n\n1. Remove all calls to `compute_logup_combinations()` within the MLE round loop. This function is currently called per-AIR per-round, producing `LogupCombinations` that are passed to `LogupMonomialBatch::new()`.\n\n2. Keep the `bus_term_sum` CPU computation (lines 568-573) since it's cheap and the monomial kernel still needs it.\n\n3. Update the call sites of `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` to pass `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` instead of `logup_combinations`.\n\n**Why:** This eliminates the 1582 precompute kernel launches and their DeviceBuffer allocations.\n\n### Change 6: Remove precompute kernel and FFI (cleanup)\n\n**Files:**\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`: Remove `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel`, `_precompute_logup_numer_combinations`, `_precompute_logup_denom_combinations` functions.\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`: Remove FFI declarations and safe wrappers for the precompute functions.\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`: Remove `LogupCombinations` struct and `compute_logup_combinations()` function.\n\n**Why:** Dead code removal. The precompute path is fully replaced by inline computation.\n\n### Change 7: Update the initial precompute overlap with Round 0\n\n**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (the `overlap-logup-precompute-round0` code path)\n\nThe existing code spawns `compute_logup_combinations()` on a background thread concurrent with Round 0. Since `compute_logup_combinations()` is being removed, this background thread no longer needs to precompute combinations. However, it still needs to:\n- Upload `d_eq_3b` per trace (this is still needed by the inline kernel)\n- Precompute `bus_term_sum` per AIR on CPU\n\nUpdate the background thread to skip the precompute kernel launches but retain the `d_eq_3b` upload and `bus_term_sum` computation. Store the `bus_term_sum` values for later use by `LogupMonomialBatch::new()`.\n\n**Why:** The background thread's precompute was overlapping with Round 0 to hide latency. With inline computation, the precompute GPU work disappears, but the `d_eq_3b` upload and CPU `bus_term_sum` computation are still needed.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: The inline combination computation must produce exactly the same `FpExt` values as the separate precompute kernel. Both paths compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t * [beta_pows[field_idx_t] if IS_DENOM])`. Verify by running all 94 tests.\n\n2. **Struct layout**: Rust `repr(C)` structs must match CUDA structs byte-for-byte. Field order and types must be identical. The `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` now has 2 extra pointer fields (16 bytes) — ensure the Rust and CUDA definitions agree on padding.\n\n3. **No regression at APC 0**: At APC 0, the monomial MLE path processes fewer monomials. The inline computation adds negligible overhead per monomial, so no regression is expected. Verify empirically.\n\n4. **Keygen data lifetime**: The `d_numer_terms` / `d_denom_terms` device buffers in `InteractionMonomials` must remain valid for the entire proof. They currently do (owned by the proving key). The monomial kernel's `d_terms` pointer must not outlive this data.\n\n5. **bus_term_sum correctness**: The CPU-computed `bus_term_sum` must still be passed correctly to `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`. This value depends on `eq_3bs` which changes per MLE round, so it must be recomputed per round.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build: `cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"` (from powdr repo)\n2. Run APC 0, 100, 300 benchmarks (from `powdr/results/pairing/`):\n   ```\n   powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apcXXX.cbor --input 0 --metrics <output>.json --recursion\n   ```\n3. Analyze with `spec.py` — focus on:\n   - MLE Rounds time at APC 300 (expect: ~106-121ms, down from 161ms)\n   - STARK excl trace at APC 300 (expect: ~1070-1085ms, down from 1125ms)\n   - APC 0 MLE Rounds (expect: no regression, ~117ms unchanged)\n4. Run nsight profile for APC 300:\n   - Verify `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel` instances = 0\n   - Verify `logup_monomial_kernel` time increase is < 5ms\n5. Run full test suite: `cargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4`\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 is < 20ms (below noise floor for this component)\n- Revert if APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by > 20ms\n- Revert if any test fails\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
