{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a plan reviewer for a GPU prover optimization project. Review the following plan following the review guideline. Return your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n\nRead these files before reviewing:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nWhen checking the current code path, verify:\n- The structs in the CUDA kernel (`LogupMonomialCtx`, `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`) at their actual file locations\n- The Rust `repr(C)` structs match the CUDA layout\n- The `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel` is actually called the way the plan says (per round, with those instance counts)\n- The `logup_monomial_kernel` accesses `d_combinations` the way described\n- The `InteractionMonomials` struct in pkey.rs has the terms arrays available\n\nAlso verify:\n- The 55ms precompute GPU time claim against the nsight profile\n- Whether the `bus_term_sum` computation depends on eq_3bs (and thus changes per round)\n- Whether Change 7 (updating the Round 0 overlap) is correct — does the background thread currently call compute_logup_combinations?\n\nBe rigorous about struct layout changes and FFI boundaries."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0156BKHSAA1fLaJTAd7AdjfB","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"606e51b1-af39-4036-8dc2-de9457beb0a9","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:09:06.269Z"}
