{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DYzfzMN1DnEJa7LifCSEgz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-1100-inline-logup-combination-precompute\n2\t\n3\tInline the `precompute_logup_combinations` GPU kernel computation into the `logup_monomial_kernel` to eliminate 1582 redundant kernel launches and ~55ms of separate GPU compute per proof. Currently, each MLE sumcheck round launches separate precompute kernels that compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t)` for every monomial, writing to intermediate buffers that the monomial evaluation kernel then reads. Since the monomial kernel already accesses the MonomialHeader (which contains `num_terms`/`term_offset`) and the required data (`d_eq_3bs`, `d_terms`) is already on the device, the combination can be computed inline with negligible overhead (~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds per monomial), eliminating the intermediate buffer allocation, the H2D/D2H traffic, and the precompute kernel launches entirely.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0156BKHSAA1fLaJTAd7AdjfB","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"84f65ca0-fc9c-469c-a746-174f2b84471c","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:09:09.962Z"}
