{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0137F3F6qBEfEB7upAToUGe1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Inline Logup Combination Precompute\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate the separate `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel` GPU launches by computing logup combination values inline within the `logup_monomial_kernel`. This targets 55ms of GPU compute time (33% of MLE Rounds) caused by 1582 tiny kernel launches that each compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t)` per monomial, writing to intermediate buffers that the monomial kernel then reads back. The monomial kernel's `MonomialHeader` already contains `num_terms`/`term_offset`, and the required data (`d_eq_3bs`, `d_terms`, `d_beta_pows`) is already on the device, so the computation can be done inline with ~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds per monomial.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Precompute phase (per MLE round, per eval group)\n10\t\n11\t1. **Rust caller** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs:509-579`): `compute_logup_combinations()` called per AIR. For each AIR:\n12\t   - Allocates `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for `d_numer_combinations` (line 524-525)\n13\t   - Allocates `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for `d_denom_combinations` (line 543-544)\n14\t   - Launches `precompute_logup_numer_combinations` FFI (line 531)\n15\t   - Launches `precompute_logup_denom_combinations` FFI (line 550)\n16\t   - Computes `bus_term_sum` on CPU (line 568-573)\n17\t\n18\t2. **CUDA kernel** (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu:304-327`): `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<IS_DENOM>` — one thread per monomial. Each thread:\n19\t   - Reads `MonomialHeader` from `headers[m]` (has `num_terms`, `term_offset`)\n20\t   - Loops over `hdr.num_terms` terms, reading `InteractionMonomialTerm` from `terms[hdr.term_offset + t]`\n21\t   - Computes `sum += eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient` (numer) or `sum += eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx] * term.coefficient * beta_pows[term.field_idx]` (denom)\n22\t   - Writes result to `out[m]`\n23\t\n24\t3. **FFI wrappers** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:1333-1363`): `precompute_logup_numer_combinations()` and `precompute_logup_denom_combinations()`.\n25\t\n26\t### Consumption phase (batch monomial MLE evaluation)\n27\t\n28\t4. **Batch setup** (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs:607-`): `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` takes `logup_combinations: &[&LogupCombinations]` and builds per-AIR `LogupMonomialCtx` structs with `d_combinations` pointer to the precomputed buffer.\n29\t\n30\t5. **CUDA kernel** (`crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu:393-442`): `logup_monomial_kernel<IS_DENOM>` — one block per (y_int, mono_block). Each thread:\n31\t   - Reads `MonomialHeader` from `ctx.d_headers[m]` (line 421) — same struct, already has `num_terms`/`term_offset`\n32\t   - Reads precomputed combination: `FpExt monomial = ctx.d_combinations[m]` (line 422)\n33\t   - Loops over `hdr.num_vars` variables, multiplying monomial by evaluated variable (lines 423-426)\n34\t   - Multiplies by `eq_xi[y_int]` and reduces (lines 427-441)\n35\t\n36\t### Data structures\n37\t\n38\t- **`MonomialHeader`** (`cuda/include/monomial.cuh:19-24`): `{var_offset: u32, term_offset: u32, num_vars: u16, num_terms: u16}` — 12 bytes. Both precompute and monomial kernels use the same struct.\n39\t- **`InteractionMonomialTerm`** (`cuda/include/monomial.cuh:37-41`): `{coefficient: Fp, interaction_idx: u16, field_idx: u16}` — 8 bytes.\n40\t- **`LogupMonomialCtx`** (`batch_mle_monomial.cu:376-381`): `{d_headers, d_variables, d_combinations, num_monomials}`.\n41\t- **`LogupMonomialCommonCtx`** (`batch_mle_monomial.cu:368-374`): `{eval_ctx, d_eq_xi, bus_term_sum, num_y, mono_blocks}`.\n42\t- **`InteractionMonomials`** (`pkey.rs:68-78`): Keygen-time data. Contains `d_numer_terms`/`d_denom_terms` (device buffers of `InteractionMonomialTerm`) that persist for the entire proof.\n43\t\n44\t### Nsight profile (APC 300)\n45\t\n46\t- `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<true>`: 35ms GPU, 791 instances, 44μs avg\n47\t- `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel<false>`: 20ms GPU, 791 instances, 25μs avg\n48\t- Total: 55ms GPU time, 1582 kernel launches\n49\t- MLE Rounds total: 161ms wall time → precompute is 34% of MLE Rounds\n50\t\n51\t## Changes\n52\t\n53\t### Change 1: Extend `LogupMonomialCtx` and `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` (CUDA)\n54\t\n55\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`\n56\t\n57\tReplace the `d_combinations` field in `LogupMonomialCtx` with `d_terms`:\n58\t\n59\t```c++\n60\tstruct LogupMonomialCtx {\n61\t    const MonomialHeader *__restrict__ d_headers;\n62\t    const PackedVar *__restrict__ d_variables;\n63\t    const InteractionMonomialTerm *__restrict__ d_terms;  // was: d_combinations\n64\t    uint32_t num_monomials;\n65\t};\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\tAdd `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` to `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`:\n69\t\n70\t```c++\n71\tstruct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n72\t    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;\n73\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_xi;\n74\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_3bs;     // NEW\n75\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_beta_pows;  // NEW (null for numer-only AIRs)\n76\t    FpExt bus_term_sum;\n77\t    uint32_t num_y;\n78\t    uint32_t mono_blocks;\n79\t};\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t**Why:** These pointers give the monomial kernel access to the data it needs to compute combinations inline. The `d_terms` pointer replaces `d_combinations` because the terms array (already on device from keygen) contains the interaction_idx and coefficient data.\n83\t\n84\t### Change 2: Inline combination computation in `logup_monomial_kernel` (CUDA)\n85\t\n86\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`\n87\t\n88\tReplace line 422 (`FpExt monomial = ctx.d_combinations[m]`) with inline computation:\n89\t\n90\t```c++\n91\t// Compute combination inline instead of reading from precomputed buffer\n92\tFpExt monomial(Fp::zero());\n93\tfor (uint16_t t = 0; t < hdr.num_terms; ++t) {\n94\t    InteractionMonomialTerm term = ctx.d_terms[hdr.term_offset + t];\n95\t    FpExt value = FpExt(term.coefficient) * common_ctx.d_eq_3bs[term.interaction_idx];\n96\t    if constexpr (IS_DENOM) {\n97\t        value *= common_ctx.d_beta_pows[term.field_idx];\n98\t    }\n99\t    monomial += value;\n100\t}\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\t**Why:** This replaces a single global memory read (`d_combinations[m]`) with 1-3 iterations of: one global memory read (`d_terms[offset+t]`) + one global memory read (`d_eq_3bs[idx]`) + 1-2 FpExt multiplications. The term data is small (8 bytes per term), and `d_eq_3bs` has high temporal locality (same indices accessed across monomials in the same AIR). The net compute overhead per monomial is ~2-4 FpExt multiply-adds, negligible compared to the variable evaluation loop (lines 423-426).\n104\t\n105\t### Change 3: Update Rust `LogupMonomialCtx` and `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` repr(C) structs\n106\t\n107\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n108\t\n109\tUpdate the Rust `LogupMonomialCtx` struct to match the new CUDA layout:\n110\t\n111\t```rust\n112\t#[repr(C)]\n113\tpub struct LogupMonomialCtx {\n114\t    pub d_headers: *const MonomialHeader,\n115\t    pub d_variables: *const PackedVar,\n116\t    pub d_terms: *const InteractionMonomialTerm<F>,  // was: d_combinations: *const EF\n117\t    pub num_monomials: u32,\n118\t}\n119\t```\n120\t\n121\tUpdate `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`:\n122\t\n123\t```rust\n124\t#[repr(C)]\n125\tpub struct LogupMonomialCommonCtx {\n126\t    pub eval_ctx: EvalCoreCtx,\n127\t    pub d_eq_xi: *const EF,\n128\t    pub d_eq_3bs: *const EF,      // NEW\n129\t    pub d_beta_pows: *const EF,   // NEW\n130\t    pub bus_term_sum: EF,\n131\t    pub num_y: u32,\n132\t    pub mono_blocks: u32,\n133\t}\n134\t```\n135\t\n136\t**Why:** Rust repr(C) structs must match the CUDA struct layout exactly for correct FFI.\n137\t\n138\t### Change 4: Update `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` to pass terms + eq_3bs instead of combinations\n139\t\n140\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n141\t\n142\tModify `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` (line ~607):\n143\t\n144\t1. Change the signature: remove `logup_combinations: &[&LogupCombinations]` parameter. Add `d_eq_3bs: &DeviceBuffer<EF>` and `d_beta_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>`.\n145\t\n146\t2. When building per-AIR `LogupMonomialCtx`, set `d_terms` from the keygen data (`pk.per_air[air_idx].other_data.interaction_monomials.d_numer_terms` / `d_denom_terms`) instead of `logup_combinations[i].d_numer_combinations`.\n147\t\n148\t3. When building `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`, set `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` from the new parameters.\n149\t\n150\t**Why:** The terms data lives in the proving key (keygen-time, persisted for the full proof). By pointing directly to this data, we avoid allocating and populating per-round combination buffers.\n151\t\n152\t### Change 5: Remove `compute_logup_combinations()` calls from MLE round loop\n153\t\n154\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs` and callers\n155\t\n156\t1. Remove all calls to `compute_logup_combinations()` within the MLE round loop. This function is currently called per-AIR per-round, producing `LogupCombinations` that are passed to `LogupMonomialBatch::new()`.\n157\t\n158\t2. Keep the `bus_term_sum` CPU computation (lines 568-573) since it's cheap and the monomial kernel still needs it.\n159\t\n160\t3. Update the call sites of `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` to pass `d_eq_3bs` and `d_beta_pows` instead of `logup_combinations`.\n161\t\n162\t**Why:** This eliminates the 1582 precompute kernel launches and their DeviceBuffer allocations.\n163\t\n164\t### Change 6: Remove precompute kernel and FFI (cleanup)\n165\t\n166\t**Files:**\n167\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.cu`: Remove `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel`, `_precompute_logup_numer_combinations`, `_precompute_logup_denom_combinations` functions.\n168\t- `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`: Remove FFI declarations and safe wrappers for the precompute functions.\n169\t- `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`: Remove `LogupCombinations` struct and `compute_logup_combinations()` function.\n170\t\n171\t**Why:** Dead code removal. The precompute path is fully replaced by inline computation.\n172\t\n173\t### Change 7: Update the initial precompute overlap with Round 0\n174\t\n175\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (the `overlap-logup-precompute-round0` code path)\n176\t\n177\tThe existing code spawns `compute_logup_combinations()` on a background thread concurrent with Round 0. Since `compute_logup_combinations()` is being removed, this background thread no longer needs to precompute combinations. However, it still needs to:\n178\t- Upload `d_eq_3b` per trace (this is still needed by the inline kernel)\n179\t- Precompute `bus_term_sum` per AIR on CPU\n180\t\n181\tUpdate the background thread to skip the precompute kernel launches but retain the `d_eq_3b` upload and `bus_term_sum` computation. Store the `bus_term_sum` values for later use by `LogupMonomialBatch::new()`.\n182\t\n183\t**Why:** The background thread's precompute was overlapping with Round 0 to hide latency. With inline computation, the precompute GPU work disappears, but the `d_eq_3b` upload and CPU `bus_term_sum` computation are still needed.\n184\t\n185\t## Invariants\n186\t\n187\t1. **Correctness**: The inline combination computation must produce exactly the same `FpExt` values as the separate precompute kernel. Both paths compute `sum_t(eq_3bs[interaction_idx_t] * coefficient_t * [beta_pows[field_idx_t] if IS_DENOM])`. Verify by running all 94 tests.\n188\t\n189\t2. **Struct layout**: Rust `repr(C)` structs must match CUDA structs byte-for-byte. Field order and types must be identical. The `LogupMonomialCommonCtx` now has 2 extra pointer fields (16 bytes) — ensure the Rust and CUDA definitions agree on padding.\n190\t\n191\t3. **No regression at APC 0**: At APC 0, the monomial MLE path processes fewer monomials. The inline computation adds negligible overhead per monomial, so no regression is expected. Verify empirically.\n192\t\n193\t4. **Keygen data lifetime**: The `d_numer_terms` / `d_denom_terms` device buffers in `InteractionMonomials` must remain valid for the entire proof. They currently do (owned by the proving key). The monomial kernel's `d_terms` pointer must not outlive this data.\n194\t\n195\t5. **bus_term_sum correctness**: The CPU-computed `bus_term_sum` must still be passed correctly to `LogupMonomialCommonCtx`. This value depends on `eq_3bs` which changes per MLE round, so it must be recomputed per round.\n196\t\n197\t## Measurement Plan\n198\t\n199\t1. Build: `cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"` (from powdr repo)\n200\t2. Run APC 0, 100, 300 benchmarks (from `powdr/results/pairing/`):\n201\t   ```\n202\t   powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apcXXX.cbor --input 0 --metrics <output>.json --recursion\n203\t   ```\n204\t3. Analyze with `spec.py` — focus on:\n205\t   - MLE Rounds time at APC 300 (expect: ~106-121ms, down from 161ms)\n206\t   - STARK excl trace at APC 300 (expect: ~1070-1085ms, down from 1125ms)\n207\t   - APC 0 MLE Rounds (expect: no regression, ~117ms unchanged)\n208\t4. Run nsight profile for APC 300:\n209\t   - Verify `precompute_logup_combinations_kernel` instances = 0\n210\t   - Verify `logup_monomial_kernel` time increase is < 5ms\n211\t5. Run full test suite: `cargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4`\n212\t\n213\t## Rollback Criteria\n214\t\n215\t- Revert if MLE Rounds improvement at APC 300 is < 20ms (below noise floor for this component)\n216\t- Revert if APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by > 20ms\n217\t- Revert if any test fails\n218\t"}]