{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UyfG2YQ5jzJ31S12zmwFsY","type":"tool_result","content":"commit a36c39869195c99729697374192054d1400c8d77\nAuthor: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>\nDate:   Tue Apr 14 17:39:56 2026 +0200\n\n    Ping-pong MLE fold buffers to eliminate per-round GPU allocations\n    \n    Pre-allocate two contiguous device buffers and alternate between them\n    during MLE fold rounds, replacing ~37K per-benchmark cudaMallocAsync\n    and ~37K cudaFreeAsync calls with zero per-round allocations.\n    \n    Key changes:\n    - Add `owns_memory` flag to DeviceBuffer enabling non-owning views\n      that skip d_free on drop\n    - Add DeviceMatrix::non_owning_view() for creating sub-region views\n    - Rewrite fold_mle_evals with fold_pingpong: reads from current\n      DeviceMatrix views, writes foldable output contiguously into the\n      alternate buffer, creates new non-owning views after swap\n    - Non-foldable (height=1) matrices retain existing views without\n      D2D copies since both ping-pong buffers stay alive\n    \n    MLE Rounds at APC 300: 171ms -> 161ms (-10ms, 1.06x)\n    STARK excl trace at APC 300: 1308ms -> 1288ms (-20ms, 1.91x vs baseline)\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n crates/cuda-backend/src/base.rs                |  14 ++\n crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs | 172 +++++++++++++++++++------\n crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs             |  29 ++++-\n 3 files changed, 177 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FpUXj5rMDdJzQNh4MtL5WB","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"c53357de-fc4d-4766-b234-4b7919c40b4a","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:25:37.462Z"}
