on-owning buffer drop safety**: Non-owning `DeviceBuffer` instances (with `owns_memory: false`) must NOT call `d_free()` on drop. This is already guaranteed by the existing `non_owning()` implementation (line 44-80 of `d_buffer.rs`).\n\n5. **Arena capacity**: The 16 MiB arena must be large enough for all WHIR Merkle digest layers across all rounds within a segment. At APC 300 with 3 WHIR rounds and max tree height 32K: total digest memory = 3 × ~2 MB = ~6 MB. 16 MiB is sufficient. If a tree requires more than 16 MiB of digest space (unlikely for this benchmark), the `alloc()` fallback returns `None` and the normal `DeviceBuffer::with_capacity()` path is used.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Build: `cargo build --bin powdr_openvm_riscv -r --features \"metrics,cuda\"` (from powdr repo)\n2. Run APC 0, 100, 300 benchmarks:\n   ```\n   powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apcXXX.cbor --input 0 --metrics <output>.json --recursion\n   ```\n3. Analyze with `spec.py` — focus on:\n   - WHIR time at APC 300 (expect: 100-115ms, down from 125ms)\n   - STARK excl trace at APC 300 (expect: 1100-1115ms, down from 1125ms)\n   - APC 0 WHIR (expect: no regression, ~218ms)\n   - LogUp GKR at APC 300 (expect: no regression, ~369ms)\n4. Run nsight profile for APC 300 to verify:\n   - poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes and merkle_tree_compress kernel times are reduced for WHIR trees\n   - No increase in cuMemCreate calls (the arena is one VPMM allocation)\n5. Run full test suite: `cargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4`\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if WHIR improvement at APC 300 is < 5ms\n- Revert if LogUp GKR at APC 300 regresses by > 10ms\n- Revert if APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by > 20ms\n- Revert if any test fails\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
