{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HCKXzVKfMdXP2suASB9MEA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-1100-whir-vpmm-arena-fold-buffers\n2\t\n3\tRecover the ~25ms WHIR regression at APC 300 by routing WHIR Merkle tree digest layer allocations through a pre-allocated VPMM-backed arena. When the VPMM page size was increased from 2 MiB to 16 MiB (task vpmm-bulk-page-creation), WHIR's Merkle tree digest layers (256 KB - 1 MB each, ~6 MB total per segment) shifted from VPMM (cuMemCreate/cuMemMap physical pages) to cudaMallocAsync (CUDA memory pool). This changed the physical memory layout for subsequent bandwidth-sensitive Poseidon2 hashing and compression kernels. Previous global page size tuning attempts failed because GKR regressed more than WHIR improved. This approach is targeted: allocate one 16 MiB VPMM-backed buffer before WHIR, sub-allocate digest layers as non-owning views within it, and free the arena after WHIR completes. No other phase's allocations are affected.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PitNSRWhugZaW1me6ZTYZB","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"1d4f0a30-160b-4524-a9ef-945d8956af73","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:31:51.990Z"}
