{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a plan reviewer for a GPU prover optimization project. Review this plan following the review guideline. Return your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n\nRead these files:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — review standard\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters/plan.md` — the plan\n\nWhen reviewing, verify:\n1. The environment variables exist in the code at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`\n2. The claimed kernel times match what's reasonable from nsight profiling\n3. The parameter sweep approach is methodical — does it cover the right ranges?\n4. The claimed mechanism is sound — do the parameters actually control what the plan says?\n5. The rollback criteria are appropriate\n\nAlso check: is there any risk that parameter changes could cause correctness issues (not just performance regression)? The plan says FoldEval and PrecomputeM produce identical results — verify this claim against the test code.\n\nBe rigorous about whether the expected impact (10-40ms on 213ms GKR inner rounds) is plausible."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D2kHotEBy4guNdSdtYdaND","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"ceecbdaf-2425-44e9-8a93-0cea761e89b8","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:38:35.339Z"}
