{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JobKURktDcRd1UF3v3TS5A","type":"tool_result","content":"autoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/report.md:29:   - Replaced the FoldEval inner loop: after round 0 (CPU), syncs sponge H2D, uploads accumulators, runs inner rounds with GPU postprocess + device-pointer compute kernels, then batch D2H + CPU transcript replay.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/report.md:58:2. **Kernel launch overhead offsets savings**: Each <<<1,1>>> postprocess kernel launch adds ~5-10μs of CPU-side overhead (driver call + kernel argument setup). Over ~20 inner rounds × 2 segments = ~0.2-0.4ms, partially offsetting any savings.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/report.md:70:- **Overlap approaches**: The FoldEval inner rounds are inherently sequential (each depends on the previous challenge), so concurrency-based approaches won't help. Focus on reducing fixed per-round overhead instead.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/plan.md:174:**Per-outer-round structure** (the key design: sync_h2d after round 0, GPU for inner rounds, replay before next outer round):\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/plan.md:187:    let inner_count = round - 1;  // number of FoldEval inner rounds\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/plan.md:292:This ensures the CPU transcript is synchronized BEFORE the next outer round's `lambda = transcript.sample_ext()` call. The replay cost is small: at most ~20 inner rounds per outer round × 16 sponge ops = ~320 sponge operations per outer round, taking ~30-50μs. Over ~20 outer rounds × 2 segments = ~1-2ms total replay overhead, which is negligible vs. the ~28ms savings.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1800-gpu-gkr-transcript-processing/plan.md:327:3. **FoldEval-only scope**: PrecomputeM rounds use the existing CPU path (with sync overhead). This ensures the optimization is safe for the initial prototype. The PrecomputeM path accounts for a minority of inner rounds (typically the last few per outer round).\nautoopt-results/log.md:215:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/log.md:295:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/task.md:3:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1430-warp-tiled-gkr-intermediates/plan.md:111:The DAG evaluation helper (`evaluate_dag_entry_gkr`) and the inner loops access intermediates via `intermediates_ptr[node * intermediate_stride]`, which now reads:\nautoopt-results/2026-04-14-1430-warp-tiled-gkr-intermediates/plan.md:126:Pass `buffer_size as u32` to the `logup_gkr_input_eval()` call. The value is already available as `rules.inner.buffer_size` (line 158).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/report.md:15:2. **Pingpong for non-final inner rounds**: For inner rounds `0..k_whir-2`, fold output goes to the pre-allocated scratch pair instead of newly allocated buffers, then `std::mem::swap` makes the scratch the \"current\" buffer. The final inner round (`k_whir-1`) still allocates correctly-sized buffers to preserve `.len() == output_height`, which `w_moments_accumulate` (cuda/whir.rs:148) reads to determine processing height.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/report.md:40:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/report.md:46:- Further WHIR improvements would require algorithmic changes (e.g., fusing sumcheck+fold into a single kernel, or reducing the number of inner rounds).\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/plan.md:5:[Omitted long matching line]\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/plan.md:40:Total VPMM allocations eliminated by the optimization: inner rounds 0-2 of WHIR round 0 (3 rounds × 2 buffers = 6 allocs) plus some from later rounds. Plus corresponding frees.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/plan.md:53:// Pre-allocate scratch buffers for pingpong fold reuse in inner rounds.\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/plan.md:54:// Capacity = initial height (2^m). Only inner rounds 0..k_whir-2 use these;\nautoopt-results/2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers/plan.md:63:### Change 2: Replace per-round allocation with pingpong for inner rounds 0..k_whir-2\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 20]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D2kHotEBy4guNdSdtYdaND","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"0c49d0c5-649c-4a0e-98f7-b6c0d143ca47","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:39:34.520Z"}
