{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012mhgvFjpTGshWXhvKe4Tsf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Tune GKR PrecomputeM Parameters\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce GKR fractional sumcheck inner round cost at APC 300 by tuning the PrecomputeM strategy's kernel launch parameters. The GKR inner rounds are the largest sequential component (213ms = 107ms per segment, 19% of STARK excl trace). The PrecomputeM strategy's `precompute_m_build_partial_kernel` (45ms, 14 instances) and `multifold_kernel` (47ms, 14 instances) are controlled by tunable parameters with existing environment variable overrides. The defaults may not be optimal for APC 300's workload (many small traces → different GKR tree shape than APC 0).\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### PrecomputeM strategy selection (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`)\n10\t\n11\t1. **Line 225-245**: `choose_round_strategy()` decides FoldEval vs PrecomputeM per GKR layer. Uses `precompute_m_min_n` (default 22 from line 36) as the minimum log-size for PrecomputeM.\n12\t\n13\t2. **Line 203-223**: `choose_precompute_m_window_w()` computes the window size (always w=3 from `GKR_WINDOW_SIZE`, line 35) and tail_tile. The tail_tile determines how many thread blocks the M-build kernel launches, computed by `precompute_m_build_tail_tile()` (lines 186-201).\n14\t\n15\t3. **Lines 186-201**: `precompute_m_build_tail_tile()` clamps `k / target_blocks` between `PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_TAIL_TILE` (256) and `PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` (4096), where k = 2^(rem_n - w) is the number of groups.\n16\t\n17\t### Environment variable overrides (lines 144-184)\n18\t\n19\t| Variable | Default | Description |\n20\t|---|---|---|\n21\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M` | enabled | Enable/disable PrecomputeM strategy |\n22\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N` | 22 | Min log-size for PrecomputeM (layers with rem_n < min_n use FoldEval) |\n23\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_BLOCKS` | 64 | Minimum blocks for M-build kernel (if fewer blocks would result, fall back to FoldEval) |\n24\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS` | 1024 | Target blocks for M-build kernel (controls tail_tile) |\n25\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` | override | Direct tail_tile override (clamped to [256, 4096]) |\n26\t\n27\t### Kernel behavior\n28\t\n29\t- **precompute_m_build_partial**: launches `num_tail_blocks` thread blocks, each processing `tail_tile` groups. More blocks = better GPU utilization but more reduction overhead.\n30\t- **multifold**: launches grid proportional to pq_size / 2^(w+pending_fold). Fixed per GKR layer.\n31\t- **frac_precompute_m_eval_round**: lightweight kernel per window sumcheck round (~0.5ms each).\n32\t\n33\t### Current profile (APC 300 nsight)\n34\t\n35\t| Kernel | GPU time | Instances | Avg |\n36\t|---|---|---|---|\n37\t| precompute_m_build_partial<true,3> | 45ms | 14 | 3.2ms |\n38\t| multifold<4> | 47ms | 14 | 3.4ms |\n39\t| compute_round_and_revert | 70ms | 141 | 0.5ms |\n40\t| bit_rev_frac_build_k2 | 50ms | 6 | 8.3ms |\n41\t| compute_round_and_fold_inplace | 9ms | 1370 | 6.6μs |\n42\t| frac_build_tree_two_layers | 12ms | 66 | 0.18ms |\n43\t| **Total GKR inner** | **~233ms** | | |\n44\t\n45\t## Changes\n46\t\n47\t### Step 1: Baseline measurement (no code changes)\n48\t\n49\tMeasure current GKR inner round time at APC 300 with default parameters. Record per-segment `logup_gkr_time_ms` and per-kernel GPU times from nsight.\n50\t\n51\t### Step 2: Parameter sweep\n52\t\n53\tUsing the existing environment variables, test the following configurations at APC 300 only (2 runs each for noise):\n54\t\n55\t**Sweep 1: TARGET_BLOCKS (controls M-build parallelism)**\n56\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=512` (fewer, larger blocks)\n57\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=2048` (more, smaller blocks)\n58\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=4096` (maximum parallelism)\n59\t\n60\tHypothesis: Higher TARGET_BLOCKS increases M-build parallelism, improving GPU utilization for the build kernel. But the reduction step also gets more expensive with more blocks.\n61\t\n62\t**Sweep 2: MIN_N (FoldEval vs PrecomputeM threshold)**\n63\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=18` (more layers use PrecomputeM)\n64\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=24` (fewer layers use PrecomputeM)\n65\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=26` (only largest layers use PrecomputeM)\n66\t\n67\tHypothesis: At APC 300, smaller GKR layers (from many small traces) may be better served by FoldEval's simpler per-round cost than PrecomputeM's M-build overhead.\n68\t\n69\t**Sweep 3: TAIL_TILE (direct block granularity)**\n70\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE=256` (minimum tile, maximum blocks)\n71\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE=1024` (moderate tile)\n72\t\n73\tHypothesis: Smaller tail tiles produce more blocks, improving parallelism for the M-build kernel on underutilized SMs.\n74\t\n75\t**Sweep 4: Disable PrecomputeM entirely**\n76\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M=0` (all layers use FoldEval)\n77\t\n78\tThis measures the FoldEval-only baseline for comparison.\n79\t\n80\t### Step 3: Identify best configuration\n81\t\n82\tFrom sweep results, identify the parameter combination that minimizes GKR inner round time at APC 300 without regressing APC 0.\n83\t\n84\t### Step 4: Verify at APC 0 and APC 100\n85\t\n86\tRun the best configuration at APC 0 and APC 100. Verify no regression beyond noise (±20ms for STARK excl trace).\n87\t\n88\t### Step 5: Apply the change\n89\t\n90\tIf a beneficial configuration is found, update the default constants in `fractional.rs`:\n91\t- `PRECOMPUTE_M_DEFAULT_TARGET_BLOCKS` (line 71)\n92\t- `PRECOMPUTE_M_DEFAULT_MIN_BLOCKS` (line 70)\n93\t- `GKR_WINDOW_DEFAULT_MIN_N` (line 36)\n94\t- `PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` (line 68) / `PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_TAIL_TILE` (line 69)\n95\t\n96\t## Invariants\n97\t\n98\t1. **Correctness**: Changing PrecomputeM parameters does not affect the mathematical result — both FoldEval and PrecomputeM produce identical sumcheck proofs (verified by existing test `test_precompute_m_multi_window_matches_fused` at line 1256). All 94 tests must pass.\n99\t\n100\t2. **No APC 0 regression**: The parameter change must not regress APC 0 STARK excl trace by > 20ms. If the optimal APC 300 config hurts APC 0, use adaptive logic (e.g., derive parameter from num_traces or total_leaves).\n101\t\n102\t3. **Parameter bounds**: TARGET_BLOCKS ≥ 1, MIN_BLOCKS ≥ 1, tail_tile ∈ [256, 4096], MIN_N ≥ GKR_WINDOW_SIZE.\n103\t\n104\t## Measurement Plan\n105\t\n106\tFor each sweep configuration:\n107\t1. Set the relevant environment variable(s)\n108\t2. Run APC 300 benchmark (from powdr repo):\n109\t   ```\n110\t   SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=<value> \\\n111\t   powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics <output>.json --recursion\n112\t   ```\n113\t3. Analyze with `spec.py` — record LogUp GKR time, STARK excl trace, and per-segment logup_gkr_time_ms.\n114\t4. For the best config: also run APC 0 and APC 100 with nsight profiling.\n115\t\n116\t## Rollback Criteria\n117\t\n118\t- Revert if no parameter combination improves GKR inner rounds at APC 300 by ≥ 10ms\n119\t- Revert if the best APC 300 config regresses APC 0 STARK excl trace by > 20ms\n120\t- Revert if any test fails\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"86e49f50-6295-49ce-925d-f1cb09489c62","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:41:57.539Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Tune GKR PrecomputeM Parameters\n\n## Goal\n\nReduce GKR fractional sumcheck inner round cost at APC 300 by tuning the PrecomputeM strategy's kernel launch parameters. The GKR inner rounds are the largest sequential component (213ms = 107ms per segment, 19% of STARK excl trace). The PrecomputeM strategy's `precompute_m_build_partial_kernel` (45ms, 14 instances) and `multifold_kernel` (47ms, 14 instances) are controlled by tunable parameters with existing environment variable overrides. The defaults may not be optimal for APC 300's workload (many small traces → different GKR tree shape than APC 0).\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### PrecomputeM strategy selection (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`)\n\n1. **Line 225-245**: `choose_round_strategy()` decides FoldEval vs PrecomputeM per GKR layer. Uses `precompute_m_min_n` (default 22 from line 36) as the minimum log-size for PrecomputeM.\n\n2. **Line 203-223**: `choose_precompute_m_window_w()` computes the window size (always w=3 from `GKR_WINDOW_SIZE`, line 35) and tail_tile. The tail_tile determines how many thread blocks the M-build kernel launches, computed by `precompute_m_build_tail_tile()` (lines 186-201).\n\n3. **Lines 186-201**: `precompute_m_build_tail_tile()` clamps `k / target_blocks` between `PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_TAIL_TILE` (256) and `PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` (4096), where k = 2^(rem_n - w) is the number of groups.\n\n### Environment variable overrides (lines 144-184)\n\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M` | enabled | Enable/disable PrecomputeM strategy |\n| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N` | 22 | Min log-size for PrecomputeM (layers with rem_n < min_n use FoldEval) |\n| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_BLOCKS` | 64 | Minimum blocks for M-build kernel (if fewer blocks would result, fall back to FoldEval) |\n| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS` | 1024 | Target blocks for M-build kernel (controls tail_tile) |\n| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` | override | Direct tail_tile override (clamped to [256, 4096]) |\n\n### Kernel behavior\n\n- **precompute_m_build_partial**: launches `num_tail_blocks` thread blocks, each processing `tail_tile` groups. More blocks = better GPU utilization but more reduction overhead.\n- **multifold**: launches grid proportional to pq_size / 2^(w+pending_fold). Fixed per GKR layer.\n- **frac_precompute_m_eval_round**: lightweight kernel per window sumcheck round (~0.5ms each).\n\n### Current profile (APC 300 nsight)\n\n| Kernel | GPU time | Instances | Avg |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| precompute_m_build_partial<true,3> | 45ms | 14 | 3.2ms |\n| multifold<4> | 47ms | 14 | 3.4ms |\n| compute_round_and_revert | 70ms | 141 | 0.5ms |\n| bit_rev_frac_build_k2 | 50ms | 6 | 8.3ms |\n| compute_round_and_fold_inplace | 9ms | 1370 | 6.6μs |\n| frac_build_tree_two_layers | 12ms | 66 | 0.18ms |\n| **Total GKR inner** | **~233ms** | | |\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Baseline measurement (no code changes)\n\nMeasure current GKR inner round time at APC 300 with default parameters. Record per-segment `logup_gkr_time_ms` and per-kernel GPU times from nsight.\n\n### Step 2: Parameter sweep\n\nUsing the existing environment variables, test the following configurations at APC 300 only (2 runs each for noise):\n\n**Sweep 1: TARGET_BLOCKS (controls M-build parallelism)**\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=512` (fewer, larger blocks)\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=2048` (more, smaller blocks)\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=4096` (maximum parallelism)\n\nHypothesis: Higher TARGET_BLOCKS increases M-build parallelism, improving GPU utilization for the build kernel. But the reduction step also gets more expensive with more blocks.\n\n**Sweep 2: MIN_N (FoldEval vs PrecomputeM threshold)**\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=18` (more layers use PrecomputeM)\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=24` (fewer layers use PrecomputeM)\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=26` (only largest layers use PrecomputeM)\n\nHypothesis: At APC 300, smaller GKR layers (from many small traces) may be better served by FoldEval's simpler per-round cost than PrecomputeM's M-build overhead.\n\n**Sweep 3: TAIL_TILE (direct block granularity)**\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE=256` (minimum tile, maximum blocks)\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE=1024` (moderate tile)\n\nHypothesis: Smaller tail tiles produce more blocks, improving parallelism for the M-build kernel on underutilized SMs.\n\n**Sweep 4: Disable PrecomputeM entirely**\n- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M=0` (all layers use FoldEval)\n\nThis measures the FoldEval-only baseline for comparison.\n\n### Step 3: Identify best configuration\n\nFrom sweep results, identify the parameter combination that minimizes GKR inner round time at APC 300 without regressing APC 0.\n\n### Step 4: Verify at APC 0 and APC 100\n\nRun the best configuration at APC 0 and APC 100. Verify no regression beyond noise (±20ms for STARK excl trace).\n\n### Step 5: Apply the change\n\nIf a beneficial configuration is found, update the default constants in `fractional.rs`:\n- `PRECOMPUTE_M_DEFAULT_TARGET_BLOCKS` (line 71)\n- `PRECOMPUTE_M_DEFAULT_MIN_BLOCKS` (line 70)\n- `GKR_WINDOW_DEFAULT_MIN_N` (line 36)\n- `PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` (line 68) / `PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_TAIL_TILE` (line 69)\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Changing PrecomputeM parameters does not affect the mathematical result — both FoldEval and PrecomputeM produce identical sumcheck proofs (verified by existing test `test_precompute_m_multi_window_matches_fused` at line 1256). All 94 tests must pass.\n\n2. **No APC 0 regression**: The parameter change must not regress APC 0 STARK excl trace by > 20ms. If the optimal APC 300 config hurts APC 0, use adaptive logic (e.g., derive parameter from num_traces or total_leaves).\n\n3. **Parameter bounds**: TARGET_BLOCKS ≥ 1, MIN_BLOCKS ≥ 1, tail_tile ∈ [256, 4096], MIN_N ≥ GKR_WINDOW_SIZE.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\nFor each sweep configuration:\n1. Set the relevant environment variable(s)\n2. Run APC 300 benchmark (from powdr repo):\n   ```\n   SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=<value> \\\n   powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics <output>.json --recursion\n   ```\n3. Analyze with `spec.py` — record LogUp GKR time, STARK excl trace, and per-segment logup_gkr_time_ms.\n4. For the best config: also run APC 0 and APC 100 with nsight profiling.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Revert if no parameter combination improves GKR inner rounds at APC 300 by ≥ 10ms\n- Revert if the best APC 300 config regresses APC 0 STARK excl trace by > 20ms\n- Revert if any test fails\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01A3go3ByfJzZy2wRaaWmRDv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BcsvqjpbBXLCea3BRVBnuL","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters/plan.md","old_string":"## Goal\n\nReduce GKR fractional sumcheck inner round cost at APC 300 by tuning the PrecomputeM strategy's kernel launch parameters. The GKR inner rounds are the largest sequential component (213ms = 107ms per segment, 19% of STARK excl trace). The PrecomputeM strategy's `precompute_m_build_partial_kernel` (45ms, 14 instances) and `multifold_kernel` (47ms, 14 instances) are controlled by tunable parameters with existing environment variable overrides. The defaults may not be optimal for APC 300's workload (many small traces → different GKR tree shape than APC 0).","new_string":"## Goal\n\nReduce GKR fractional sumcheck inner round cost at APC 300 by tuning the PrecomputeM strategy parameters, primarily the `MIN_N` threshold that controls which GKR layers use PrecomputeM vs FoldEval. The GKR inner rounds are the largest sequential component (213ms = 107ms per segment, 19% of STARK excl trace). The directly tunable kernel is `precompute_m_build_partial_kernel` (45ms total). The `multifold_kernel` (47ms) has fixed launch geometry unaffected by these parameters, but can be eliminated entirely for layers shifted to FoldEval via `MIN_N`. The MIN_N sweep is the primary optimization vector: raising it from 22 to 24-26 could shift 2-4 layers from PrecomputeM to FoldEval, eliminating their M-build + reduction + multifold overhead (~6.6ms per layer). The TARGET_BLOCKS and TAIL_TILE sweeps are secondary, targeting the M-build kernel's GPU utilization for layers that remain on PrecomputeM."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creatio