{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a plan reviewer for a GPU prover optimization project. This is a re-review after incorporating feedback from the first review. Check whether the design-level concerns were addressed.\n\nRead:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — review standard\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters/plan.md` — the updated plan\n\nThe first review found NO design-level blockers but raised concerns about:\n1. Inflated impact claim (45ms vs 92ms budget) — the multifold kernel is unaffected by TARGET_BLOCKS/TAIL_TILE tuning\n2. Sweep order — MIN_N sweep should be front-loaded as the primary vector\n3. Missing diagnostic step — should log per-layer strategy decisions before sweeping\n4. Missing combined sweeps — should test best combination\n5. Reduction kernel cost scaling with TARGET_BLOCKS\n\nCheck whether these were addressed in the update. Return: Findings, Improvements, Assessment."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GaMaq4FidjHtz9iRdQaBWX","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"433bf134-1330-4903-9180-8e7241c3d4ed","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:42:37.710Z"}
