{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019KCK3Hugumd2RDJuMBZ71A","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Tune GKR PrecomputeM Parameters\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce GKR fractional sumcheck inner round cost at APC 300 by tuning the PrecomputeM strategy parameters, primarily the `MIN_N` threshold that controls which GKR layers use PrecomputeM vs FoldEval. The GKR inner rounds are the largest sequential component (213ms = 107ms per segment, 19% of STARK excl trace). The directly tunable kernel is `precompute_m_build_partial_kernel` (45ms total). The `multifold_kernel` (47ms) has fixed launch geometry unaffected by these parameters, but can be eliminated entirely for layers shifted to FoldEval via `MIN_N`. The MIN_N sweep is the primary optimization vector: raising it from 22 to 24-26 could shift 2-4 layers from PrecomputeM to FoldEval, eliminating their M-build + reduction + multifold overhead (~6.6ms per layer). The TARGET_BLOCKS and TAIL_TILE sweeps are secondary, targeting the M-build kernel's GPU utilization for layers that remain on PrecomputeM.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### PrecomputeM strategy selection (`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs`)\n10\t\n11\t1. **Line 225-245**: `choose_round_strategy()` decides FoldEval vs PrecomputeM per GKR layer. Uses `precompute_m_min_n` (default 22 from line 36) as the minimum log-size for PrecomputeM.\n12\t\n13\t2. **Line 203-223**: `choose_precompute_m_window_w()` computes the window size (always w=3 from `GKR_WINDOW_SIZE`, line 35) and tail_tile. The tail_tile determines how many thread blocks the M-build kernel launches, computed by `precompute_m_build_tail_tile()` (lines 186-201).\n14\t\n15\t3. **Lines 186-201**: `precompute_m_build_tail_tile()` clamps `k / target_blocks` between `PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_TAIL_TILE` (256) and `PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` (4096), where k = 2^(rem_n - w) is the number of groups.\n16\t\n17\t### Environment variable overrides (lines 144-184)\n18\t\n19\t| Variable | Default | Description |\n20\t|---|---|---|\n21\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M` | enabled | Enable/disable PrecomputeM strategy |\n22\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N` | 22 | Min log-size for PrecomputeM (layers with rem_n < min_n use FoldEval) |\n23\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_BLOCKS` | 64 | Minimum blocks for M-build kernel (if fewer blocks would result, fall back to FoldEval) |\n24\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS` | 1024 | Target blocks for M-build kernel (controls tail_tile) |\n25\t| `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` | override | Direct tail_tile override (clamped to [256, 4096]) |\n26\t\n27\t### Kernel behavior\n28\t\n29\t- **precompute_m_build_partial**: launches `num_tail_blocks` thread blocks, each processing `tail_tile` groups. More blocks = better GPU utilization but more reduction overhead.\n30\t- **multifold**: launches grid proportional to pq_size / 2^(w+pending_fold). Fixed per GKR layer.\n31\t- **frac_precompute_m_eval_round**: lightweight kernel per window sumcheck round (~0.5ms each).\n32\t\n33\t### Current profile (APC 300 nsight)\n34\t\n35\t| Kernel | GPU time | Instances | Avg |\n36\t|---|---|---|---|\n37\t| precompute_m_build_partial<true,3> | 45ms | 14 | 3.2ms |\n38\t| multifold<4> | 47ms | 14 | 3.4ms |\n39\t| compute_round_and_revert | 70ms | 141 | 0.5ms |\n40\t| bit_rev_frac_build_k2 | 50ms | 6 | 8.3ms |\n41\t| compute_round_and_fold_inplace | 9ms | 1370 | 6.6μs |\n42\t| frac_build_tree_two_layers | 12ms | 66 | 0.18ms |\n43\t| **Total GKR inner** | **~233ms** | | |\n44\t\n45\t## Changes\n46\t\n47\t### Step 1: Baseline measurement (no code changes)\n48\t\n49\tMeasure current GKR inner round time at APC 300 with default parameters. Record per-segment `logup_gkr_time_ms` and per-kernel GPU times from nsight.\n50\t\n51\t### Step 1.5: Diagnostic — log per-layer strategy decisions\n52\t\n53\tAdd temporary `tracing::info!` in `choose_round_strategy()` (line 225) to log `(round, rem_n, strategy)` for each GKR outer round. Run once at APC 300 to determine:\n54\t- How many layers use PrecomputeM vs FoldEval\n55\t- What `rem_n` values the PrecomputeM layers have\n56\t- The improvement ceiling (number of layers × ~6.6ms per eliminated PrecomputeM layer)\n57\t\n58\tThis diagnostic directly informs which sweep ranges are productive.\n59\t\n60\t### Step 2: Parameter sweep\n61\t\n62\tUsing the existing environment variables, test configurations at APC 300 (2 runs each for noise). **Front-load Sweep 2 (MIN_N)** since it has the highest probability of impact.\n63\t\n64\t**Sweep 2 (primary): MIN_N (FoldEval vs PrecomputeM threshold)**\n65\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=24` (fewer layers use PrecomputeM)\n66\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=26` (only largest layers use PrecomputeM)\n67\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N=28` (almost all layers use FoldEval)\n68\t\n69\tHypothesis: At APC 300, smaller GKR layers (from many small traces) may be better served by FoldEval's simpler per-round cost than PrecomputeM's M-build + reduction + multifold overhead (~6.6ms per layer). Raising MIN_N shifts these layers to FoldEval, eliminating both `precompute_m_build_partial` and `multifold` invocations for those layers.\n70\t\n71\t**Sweep 1 (secondary, only if Sweep 2 shows promise): TARGET_BLOCKS**\n72\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=512` (fewer, larger blocks)\n73\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=2048` (more, smaller blocks)\n74\t\n75\tHypothesis: Higher TARGET_BLOCKS increases M-build parallelism but the `precompute_m_reduce_partials_kernel` iterates over `num_blocks` in a serial loop per thread, so more blocks increases reduction cost linearly. Net effect is unclear; only test if Sweep 2 leaves PrecomputeM layers that could benefit.\n76\t\n77\t**Sweep 3 (secondary): TAIL_TILE (direct block granularity)**\n78\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE=256` (minimum tile, maximum blocks)\n79\t\n80\tNote: TAIL_TILE override bypasses TARGET_BLOCKS computation (line 193-194). Only test independently from Sweep 1.\n81\t\n82\t**Sweep 4: Disable PrecomputeM entirely**\n83\t- `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M=0` (all layers use FoldEval)\n84\t\n85\tFoldEval-only baseline for comparison. Establishes the maximum possible savings from eliminating all PrecomputeM overhead.\n86\t\n87\t**Sweep 5 (combined): Best MIN_N + best TARGET_BLOCKS**\n88\tTest the best MIN_N value from Sweep 2 combined with the best TARGET_BLOCKS from Sweep 1 (if applicable).\n89\t\n90\t### Step 3: Identify best configuration\n91\t\n92\tFrom sweep results, identify the parameter combination that minimizes GKR inner round time at APC 300 without regressing APC 0.\n93\t\n94\t### Step 4: Verify at APC 0 and APC 100\n95\t\n96\tRun the best configuration at APC 0 and APC 100. Verify no regression beyond noise (±20ms for STARK excl trace).\n97\t\n98\t### Step 5: Apply the change\n99\t\n100\tIf a beneficial configuration is found, update the default constants in `fractional.rs`:\n101\t- `PRECOMPUTE_M_DEFAULT_TARGET_BLOCKS` (line 71)\n102\t- `PRECOMPUTE_M_DEFAULT_MIN_BLOCKS` (line 70)\n103\t- `GKR_WINDOW_DEFAULT_MIN_N` (line 36)\n104\t- `PRECOMPUTE_M_TAIL_TILE` (line 68) / `PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_TAIL_TILE` (line 69)\n105\t\n106\t## Invariants\n107\t\n108\t1. **Correctness**: Changing PrecomputeM parameters does not affect the mathematical result — both FoldEval and PrecomputeM produce identical sumcheck proofs (verified by existing test `test_precompute_m_multi_window_matches_fused` at line 1256). All 94 tests must pass.\n109\t\n110\t2. **No APC 0 regression**: The parameter change must not regress APC 0 STARK excl trace by > 20ms. If the optimal APC 300 config hurts APC 0, use adaptive logic (e.g., derive parameter from num_traces or total_leaves).\n111\t\n112\t3. **Parameter bounds**: TARGET_BLOCKS ≥ 1, MIN_BLOCKS ≥ 1, tail_tile ∈ [256, 4096], MIN_N ≥ GKR_WINDOW_SIZE.\n113\t\n114\t## Measurement Plan\n115\t\n116\tFor each sweep configuration:\n117\t1. Set the relevant environment variable(s)\n118\t2. Run APC 300 benchmark (from powdr repo):\n119\t   ```\n120\t   SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_TARGET_BLOCKS=<value> \\\n121\t   powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics <output>.json --recursion\n122\t   ```\n123\t3. Analyze with `spec.py` — record LogUp GKR time, STARK excl trace, and per-segment logup_gkr_time_ms.\n124\t4. For the best config: also run APC 0 and APC 100 with nsight profiling.\n125\t\n126\t## Rollback Criteria\n127\t\n128\t- Revert if no parameter combination improves GKR inner rounds at APC 300 by ≥ 10ms\n129\t- Revert if the best APC 300 config regresses APC 0 STARK excl trace by > 20ms\n130\t- Revert if any test fails\n131\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GaMaq4FidjHtz9iRdQaBWX","session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"3b009929-43b1-4305-9fb0-00d54be50974","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:42:40.994Z"}
