{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MLtPDVjWX4JaAApAE3pKep","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters\n\nTune the GKR fractional sumcheck PrecomputeM strategy parameters (`TARGET_BLOCKS`, `MIN_BLOCKS`, `MIN_N`, `TAIL_TILE`) to reduce the GKR inner round cost at APC 300. The GKR inner rounds are the single largest sequential component at 213ms (107ms per segment), with `precompute_m_build_partial` at 45ms and `multifold` at 47ms being the dominant kernels. The current defaults (`TARGET_BLOCKS=1024`, `MIN_BLOCKS=64`, `MIN_N=22`, `TAIL_TILE=4096`) were set without specific tuning for the APC 300 workload, which has a different GKR tree shape (more traces, smaller per-trace) than APC 0. Parameter sweeping via the existing `SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_*` environment variables can identify a configuration that better balances GPU parallelism and per-window overhead for this workload.\n=== plan.md exists ===\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 georg georg 7943 Apr 16 11:42 /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters/plan.md\n=== no source code modified ===","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78bbe79a-49aa-4ea3-b7e0-2913b403757d","uuid":"4d3f2d17-bd3c-4a56-9ead-b32a1c680b10","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:43:49.758Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-16-1100-tune-gkr-precompute-m-parameters\n\nTune the GKR fractional sumcheck PrecomputeM strategy parameters (`TARGET_BLOCKS`, `MIN_BLOCKS`, `MIN_N`, `TAIL_TILE`) to reduce the GKR inner round cost at APC 300. The GKR inner rounds are the single largest sequential component at 213ms (107ms per segment), with `precompute_m_build_partial` at 45ms and `multifold` at 47ms being the dominant kernels. The current defaults (`TARGET_BLOCKS=1024`, `MIN_BLOCKS=64`, `MIN_N=22`, `TAIL_TILE=4096`) were set without specific tuning for the APC 300 workload, which has a different G